Title: One type field, one frontmatter shape, valid_while and supersedes
Created: 2026-09-10
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-09-10T15:50Z claude created

--- body ---

## Context

Ranking reads frontmatter, and the frontmatter is not uniform enough to rank
on: 47 bodies carry no type field, and two shapes are in use (`type:` at top
level versus `metadata.type`). Separately, nothing declares when a memory stops
being true — the TTL table meant to handle it gives `feedback`, 74% of the
corpus, no threshold at all.

The replacement is a declared, executable condition. A memory says what it is
true *while*: a path exists, a pattern is still present in a named file, a tool
is below a version. Expiry only unranks, so it is **reversible** — a tool that
regresses revives its memory at the next pass with no human action.

Design reference: defects 3 and 4, principle P3, ticket T3 in `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md`.

## Relevant files

- `skills/memory/SKILL.md` — the write path and the TTL table this replaces
- `skills/dream/provenance.py` — where the scorer will call the resolver
- `projects/*/memory/*.md` — the 47 untyped bodies and the two shapes

## Actions

1. Normalise: one type field, one frontmatter shape, every body typed.
2. Define `valid_while` as a **closed** grammar — path exists, pattern present
   in a named file, tool below a version — and reject anything else. Prose in
   this field degrades into a comment nothing can check.
3. Check it at both ends, failing differently:
   - **At writing, fail closed.** The predicate must parse, evaluate, and
     evaluate *true*. A memory born expired can never rank, so it is an error,
     not a record. The author is present and can fix it.
   - **At scoring, fail open and report.** An unevaluable predicate leaves the
     entry valid and raises a lint. Nobody is present, and a silent expiry
     loses a lesson for a reason no one will ever see.
4. Add `supersedes`, naming a slug; the generator refuses to rank both.

Do not harmonise the two failure modes. Fail closed where a human can fix it,
fail open where none can.

## Test

Red first, one per rule: a malformed predicate rejected at write; a
false-at-write predicate rejected; an unevaluable predicate at scoring leaving
the entry ranked *and* producing a lint line; a false predicate unranking; the
same predicate becoming true again and the entry returning.

## Verification

- [ ] No body lacks a type; one shape survives
- [ ] The grammar rejects a prose condition
- [ ] A revived entry reappears with no human action

## Invariants

- Expiry never deletes. It unranks.
- The scorer stays deterministic: no model judges validity.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] 47 untyped bodies typed; one frontmatter shape
- [ ] `valid_while` accepts the closed grammar and nothing else
- [ ] Write-time rejection and scoring-time valid-and-report, both tested
- [ ] `supersedes` prevents both entries ranking
